Simple Analogy

Think of a 500-page textbook.

If someone asks:

"What is recursion?"

You don't read all 500 pages.

Instead, you:

Open the index.
Go to the relevant chapter.
Read only those pages.

Chunking works the same way. It divides a large document into smaller sections so the system can quickly find and use only the relevant information.

In one sentence

Chunking is the process of breaking a large document into smaller, searchable pieces so an AI system can retrieve the most relevant information 
efficiently and accurately.

